// Syncthing ignore for Obsidian vault — same file on Mac and WSL
// Copy to: ~/Documents/Obsidian/.stignore

// Obsidian internals
.obsidian
.trash

// OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

// Editor temp files
*.swp
*.swo
*~

// Syncthing metadata (don't sync its own state)
.stfolder
.stversions

// Git repos inside vault (if any)
.git

// Node/build artifacts (if any tools run inside vault)
node_modules

// CEO runtime files that are machine-local (not vault state).
//
// The per-trigger cron state below moved to $HOME/.ceo/state/ in #394 — a host
// running current code writes none of these paths. They stay as coverage for the
// files an upgrading host still has lying around before its first run migrates
// them, and because nothing guarantees every host is on current code at once.
//
// They are not the protection any more, which was the point of moving them: this
// file only protects a host that copied it into its vault root, and nothing
// verifies that copy. On 2026-09-09 both swarm hosts were found running an August
// copy with no rule for a file added since.
CEO/log/.last-run-*
CEO/log/.retry-*.json
CEO/log/.config-hash
// Trailing * is load-bearing: #299 renamed the single .fail-count to
// .fail-count-<trigger>, and the bare pattern silently stopped matching, so
// every per-trigger counter synced between hosts. That reintroduced the exact
// bug #299 fixed — one host's healthy run zeroing another's failure streak —
// one level up. ceo-stignore-coverage.test.sh now enforces the coverage.
CEO/log/.fail-count*
// The dispatcher's completion log. Every host appended to one shared
// CEO/log/cron-runs.log, which Syncthing forks rather than merges: ten
// .sync-conflict copies by 2026-09-09 (#397). It is host-local runtime state
// like the counters above, so it should never have synced. #397 also keys the
// file by host (cron-runs-<host>.log); the glob covers both names and the
// conflict copies already in the vault.
CEO/log/cron-runs*.log
CEO/log/.last-scan
CEO/log/.from-nathan-seen
CEO/log/.nathan-nb-counter
// --dry-run preview output is host-local scratch (see ceo-cron.sh --dry-run)
CEO/log/preview/
// registry.json is host-local — it now lives at ~/.ceo/registry.json (each host
// regenerates its own via `ceo playbook scan`). Two hosts scanning a synced copy
// would both rewrite it and produce .sync-conflict files. Ignore any stale copy
// lingering in the vault from before the swarm migration; nothing should sync it.
// (CEO/swarm.json and CEO/heartbeats/ DO sync — they describe the swarm, not one host.)
CEO/registry.json
